WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.950
Medmerry lies just west
of Selsey, in West Sussex.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.790
By 2014, the Environment Agency had built
7 kilometres of new embankments there.

3
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:14.970
At the time, the 28 million pound project
was described as the largest open-coast

4
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.910
scheme in Europe.

5
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.830
Then the sea was let in,
to flood the land between.

6
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.750
Why spend millions to
give land to the sea?

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.770
Was the land simply worthless?

8
00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:28.950
In this mission, you'll weigh
four options for any coast:

9
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.190
hold the line, advance it,
realign it, or do nothing.

10
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.750
Then you'll judge hard
and soft engineering,

11
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.390
from groynes to the sea wall at Ventnor.

12
00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:44.930
Your mission: explain why the Environment
Agency gave land to the sea at Medmerry.
